/** @page protobuferrorsguide Error Reference

    @tableofcontents

    |!Exception|!Description
    |\c PROTOBUF-SCHEMA-ERROR|Schema loading, parsing, or building failed, or a path, file name, or a name, type, or label in a schema definition contains a NUL character
    |\c PROTOBUF-TYPE-ERROR|Message or enum type not found in schema, or a type name contains a NUL character
    |\c PROTOBUF-FIELD-ERROR|Unknown field name in hash during encoding
    |\c PROTOBUF-ENCODE-ERROR|Protobuf serialization failed
    |\c PROTOBUF-DECODE-ERROR|Protobuf binary parsing failed, or a string map key in a message decoded or parsed from JSON contains a NUL character, which a hash key cannot hold
    |\c PROTOBUF-JSON-ERROR|JSON conversion or parsing failed
    |\c INVALID-ENCODING|A string field or a string map key of a \c proto2 message decoded from binary data is not valid UTF-8 (a \c proto3 message with one fails to parse: \c PROTOBUF-DECODE-ERROR), or the JSON text given to \c ProtobufSchema::fromJson() is not valid text in its encoding; the description names the method (ex: \c "ProtobufSchema::decode()")
    |\c PROTOBUF-DEPTH-ERROR|A message to convert to or from a hash has message fields nested more than 100 levels below the top-level message (see @ref protobufnesting)
    |\c PROTOBUF-SYMBOL-NOT-FOUND|Symbol not found in schema (descriptor serialization), or the symbol contains a NUL character
    |\c PROTOBUF-FILE-NOT-FOUND|Proto file not found in schema (descriptor serialization), or the file name contains a NUL character
*/
